.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt USERMOD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm usermod
.Nd modify an existing user account
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l Ar NEW_LOGIN
.Op Fl u Ar UID Op Fl o
.Op Fl g Ar GROUP
.Op Fl G Ar LIST Op Fl a
.Op Fl d Ar HOMEDIR Op Fl m
.Op Fl s Ar SHELL
.Op Fl c Ar COMMENT
.Op Fl L | Fl U
.Ar USER
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
edits the
.Pa /etc/passwd
entry for
.Ar USER
in place, with side effects in
.Pa /etc/shadow
(for renames and lock/unlock) and
.Pa /etc/group
(for primary-group changes, supplementary-group lists, and renames
that appear in member rolls).
.Pp
Each affected database file is rewritten atomically; the lock file at
.Pa /etc/.pwd.lock
serialises against concurrent admin tools.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l Ar NEW_LOGIN
Rename the account.  Updates
.Pa /etc/passwd ,
.Pa /etc/shadow ,
and every supplementary-member reference in
.Pa /etc/group .
Files inside the home directory are
.Em not
renamed.
.It Fl u Ar UID Op Fl o
Change the UID.  Files in the home directory owned by the old UID are
.Em not
.Xr chown 2 Ns ed
automatically.  Pass
.Fl o
to permit a non-unique UID.
.It Fl g Ar GROUP
Change the primary group (named or numeric).  Must exist.
.It Fl G Ar LIST
Replace the supplementary-group set with
.Ar LIST .
With
.Fl a ,
append rather than replace.
.It Fl a
With
.Fl G ,
append to the existing supplementary set instead of replacing it.
.It Fl d Ar HOMEDIR Op Fl m
Change the home-directory field.  With
.Fl m ,
attempt to rename the existing home into the new path
.Pq same filesystem only \(em cross-fs moves are not implemented .
.It Fl s Ar SHELL
Change the login shell.
.It Fl c Ar COMMENT
Change the GECOS field.
.It Fl L
Lock the account by prefixing the shadow hash with
.Sq \&! .
.It Fl U
Unlock the account by stripping a leading
.Sq \&! .
.El
.Fl L
and
.Fl U
are mutually exclusive.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Same as
.Xr useradd 8 :
0 success, 2 bad usage, 3 bad value, 4 UID clash, 6 group missing,
9 name in use, 10 database write failed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr shadow 5 ,
.Xr useradd 8 ,
.Xr userdel 8 ,
.Xr groupmod 8
.Sh AUTHORS
Substrate-native
.Nm ,
written to match the shadow-utils command-line surface.
